{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "15", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "06", "M": "17", "S": "25"}}, "news": [{"title": "Punjab begins mapping legitimate raw material supply for stone crushers", "para": "The Punjab Pollution Control Board is currently evaluating legitimate sources of raw materials for stone crushers. This scrutiny is designed to guarantee adherence to state regulations and policies. In the Ropar district, a significant number of stone crushers obtain materials from Punjab, Haryana, and Himachal Pradesh. Alarmingly, over 42% of these units have been found to violate pollution control laws.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/allied-industries/punjab-begins-mapping-legitimate-raw-material-supply-for-stone-crushers/133255470?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-280776/133255470.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "allied-industries"}, {"title": "After Mumbai, Pune set for plot-wise ready reckoner rates under micro-zoning", "para": "Pune and Mumbai are set to implement a detailed property valuation system that will transition from broad zoning classifications to more specific rates tied to individual plots and buildings. The state registration department is gearing up to adjust property rates for the upcoming year while introducing reforms like new stamp duty offices and mandatory land measurement. Additionally, linking Aadhaar may be required for all document registrations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/after-mumbai-pune-set-for-plot-wise-ready-reckoner-rates-under-micro-zoning/133254987?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-76444/133254987.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Gujarat government mulls higher FSI, taller buildings in GIDCs", "para": "The Gujarat government is set to enhance the floor space index for industrial plots located within GIDC estates. Building height regulations will be adjusted based on road width, permitting taller constructions. This initiative is designed to support vertical growth in several manufacturing industries. Industry representatives have persistently called for these updates in response to evolving economic realities, and the proposed changes invite public feedback for consideration.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/gujarat-government-mulls-higher-fsi-taller-buildings-in-gidcs/133254952?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-235520/133254952.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}